  "definition": "Ketamine is a drug with pain-relieving and anesthetic effects that can also cause sedation. Its actions are complex and not fully understood, but they appear to include effects on NMDA receptors, opioid receptors, and biogenic amine uptake, which may help reduce pain perception.",
